  "held_fixed": "icosphere, uniform random sampling, 60000 samples",
  "mechanism_under_test": "_support takes the maximum vertex distance over each triangle, so a coarse triangle reaches further from its nearest sample than a fine one covering the same surface. Coarse meshes should report more unsupported area everywhere, compressing the share's range and raising the floor.",
  "question": "Resolution did not explain the gap between my floor near 0.017 and the review lane's 0.09: the floor stayed flat across edge/voxel 0.705 to 22.467. The remaining difference is the voxel convention. Every measurement in this tree used the tool's own voxel = 2x median nearest-neighbour spacing, which puts the zero-error unsupported fraction near 0.17; the review lane reported 0.75126, which implies a tighter voxel. This varies that multiple.",
